{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>Write this for a memorial in the book</b>. Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 17:14) that it is a known book, namely \"the Book of the Wars of YHWH\" (Numbers 21:14), and written in it are the wars that HaShem waged for those who fear Him, and it is possible that it existed from the days of Abraham. But there is nothing in his words here except a guess. And the correct interpretation in my eyes is that <b>\"in the book\"</b> alludes to the Book of the Torah, as in the matter that is written (Deuteronomy 31:26), \"Take this book of the Torah\" — He says: write this in the book of My Torah, so that Israel will remember what Amalek did, for I will utterly erase his remembrance and I will place my vengeance upon him through the hand of My people Israel. And this is the commandment written for us in Mishneh Torah (Deuteronomy 25:17): \"Remember what Amalek did to you.\" And He said, <b>and put it in the ears of Joshua</b>, to command him to remind Israel of all the trouble that came upon them through him, for he is one who knows and is a witness, and it alludes that after they inherit the land they will erase him, for the commandment upon them first is to destroy the seven nations and inherit the land — this is what is stated there (Deuteronomy 25:19), \"And it shall be when YHWH your Elohim gives you rest,\" etc. And if this had been in the days of Joshua son of Nun, he would have warned them to erase him, but there remained much land to inherit in his days (Joshua 13:1), and its time did not come until the reign of Saul."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:17:02.421196380Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}